Second Announcement

The Journal of Universal Language  - Calls for Papers=20

Honorarium: as a token of our gratitude, the authors whose paper=20
     will appear in the journal of universal language
     will be given around $900-$1,000.=20

Topic Areas: The journal of universal language is concerned with=20
      various areas of artificial language, universality=20
      in language, communication & culture in language,=20
      endangered language, and language typology.=20
      The editors encourage the submission of papers on=20
      proposed themes as well as on other topics relevant=20
      to the interest of the journal of universal language.=20
      Each volume contains two issues, published in march=20
      and september. The language of publication is english.=20

Format: 1. The length of manuscripts should not exceed 25 pages.=20
        2. A 200-word abstract should be given at the beginning of=20
        manuscripts.=20
        3. Manuscripts should be submitted on a4 paper, with the=20
        margins of at least  4cm on all four sides of each sheet.=20
        They may be single-spaced and/or double-sided, if desired.   =
=20

Important Dates:
       Submission Deadline: December 31, 2001
              Notification of Acceptance: January 31, 2002
              Submission of Camera-Ready Papers: February 28, 2002
Submission:=20
        1. Electronic submissions are acceptable.  Acceptable file
        formats are postscript (.ps), portable document format (.pdf),=20
        ms word (.doc), and plain text. please send your file in an=20
        attachment to jytak@sejong.ac.kr.
        2. For hard copy submissions, please send 3 copies, accompanied=20
        by a cover letter which includes the author's name, affiliation,=20
        address, and home or office phone number, to:
=20=20=20=20=20=20
